# Goal

Add an experimental, opt-in `greetingInterruption?: false | true | BrowserVadOptions` path to `OpenAIAdapter`. During a fixed greeting, locally accepted speech must stop local greeting audio first, then publish one bounded `LocalAudioPreRoll` tail before live microphone samples. Omitted or `false` configuration must retain the current raw-track attachment and non-interruptible greeting gate. Any runtime VAD or AudioWorklet failure must keep voice connected, discard greeting-period audio, and use that existing gate. Explicit **Skip greeting** remains the reliable control.

The change must remain narrow. OpenAI still owns normal turn detection and response behavior after the greeting. `GreetingPresentation` composes a package-private interruption owner. `OpenAIAdapter` only asks presentation to prepare the publication track, attaches that track, and delegates greeting and teardown lifecycle.

# Phases

## Phase 1 — Deliver the opt-in greeting interruption slice

### Intent

Expose the validated option and implement one complete enabled path from microphone capture through local greeting interruption. Keep disabled construction and connection on the current path.

