# Definition of done

- The public option is typed, documented, synchronously validated when enabled, and disabled by default.
- Disabled behavior attaches and gates the raw microphone exactly as before and performs no VAD/worklet setup.
- Enabled behavior attaches one owner-managed generated track, stops greeting playback before one bounded pre-roll flush, then carries live audio.
- Normal completion and Skip discard greeting-period audio before restoring live publication.
- Runtime experimental failures safely retain the old non-interruptible gate and do not fail voice or leak greeting-period audio.
- Greeting history remains at most once in Engine and OpenAI, and immediate/transcript-confirmed response behavior remains unchanged after greeting settlement.
- Cleanup is exact across success, failure, disconnect, replacement, and reconnect generations. Raw-stream metering remains unchanged.
- Direct owner, adapter, race, fallback, teardown, default-off, docs fixture, and acoustic-uncertainty coverage is green.
- The demo remains explicitly disabled.
- The real-device matrix remains **Not tested** until actual hardware evidence exists.
- All listed package, demo, docs, public API, and root non-browser verification commands pass.
